  ],
  "answer": "<p>The correct option is <b>Database Migration Service with continuous replication for PostgreSQL</b>. This service supports large PostgreSQL migrations by seeding the target and then continuously replicating changes so you can achieve very low downtime at cutover. <b>Database Migration Service with continuous replication for PostgreSQL</b> supports ongoing changes during replication and provides validation features that let you compare source and destination before cutover. You can keep the source as the system of record until you are satisfied with validation which preserves a clear path to roll back by continuing to use the source if issues appear.</p><p>With <b>Database Migration Service with continuous replication for PostgreSQL</b> you can run a continuous migration that keeps the destination closely synchronized while users continue to modify data. It is designed for large datasets such as 18 TB and it provides migration status and data validation to confirm row counts and checksums which reduces risk before switching traffic. Because cutover is a simple and reversible step while the source is still active you retain the option to back out if needed.</p><p><i>Cloud Data Fusion</i> is a data integration and ETL service that builds pipelines for batch or streaming use cases. It is not a managed database migration tool for low downtime lift and shift of a transactional PostgreSQL database and it does not provide a controlled cutover workflow with continuous logical replication.</p><p><i>Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL</i> is the managed database that serves as the migration target rather than the migration mechanism. It does not by itself perform replication from on premises or provide the end to end migration workflow that includes validation and cutover.</p><p><i>Datastream</i> is a change data capture service focused on moving data into analytics oriented sinks such as BigQuery or Cloud Storage. It is not designed for migrating a PostgreSQL database into a managed PostgreSQL instance with a minimal downtime cutover and rollback plan.</p>",
